The examples in this directory are described in the userguide.


Short description
-----------------

stick_slip1:

 Axisymmetrical viscoelastic "stick-slip" problem:
 1) An entry problem with a parabolic velocity profile and zero stress.
 2) At some point on the upper boundary the fixed wall changes into
    a perfectly slipping wall (no friction).
 3) At the outflow zero stress is assumed.
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 first-order time integration

stick_slip2:

 Axisymmetrical viscoelastic "stick-slip" problem:
 1) An internal periodic boundary at the entry of the domain on the left.
 2) At some point on the upper boundary the fixed wall changes into
    a perfectly slipping wall (no friction).
 3) At the outflow zero stress is assumed.
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 first-order time integration

stick_slip3:

 Axisymmetrical viscoelastic "stick-slip" problem:
 1) An open boundary at the entry of the domain on the left.
 2) At some point on the upper boundary the fixed wall changes into
    a perfectly slipping wall (no friction).
 3) At the outflow zero stress is assumed.
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 first-order time integration

stick_slip4:

 Axisymmetrical viscoelastic "stick-slip" problem:
 1) An open boundary at the entry of the domain on the left.
 2) At some point on the upper boundary the fixed wall changes into
    a perfectly slipping wall (no friction).
 3) At the outflow zero stress is assumed.
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 Implicit bilinear terms of CE in momentum balance.
 second-order Gear time integration/conformation prediction
